#: ../fhir-harness/processes/content/l3-fhir-pipeline.bpmn:62
#. Diagram label
msgid "Source model ready"
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/processes/content/l3-fhir-pipeline.bpmn:35
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Task_AuthorFsh is the single re-entry point for both failure paths: an invalid-FHIR loop from Gateway_Valid, which leaves no record, and a QC failure, which arrives after Task_QcBeans has filed it. Which edge fired is the only signal that tells a mechanical re-run from a finding to read."
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/processes/content/l3-fhir-pipeline.bpmn:63
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The IG's source model is ready: l3-fhir-authoring's required sourceModel. Which model, and how it was produced, is the calling process's to say; this pipeline names none."
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/processes/content/l3-fhir-pipeline.bpmn:56
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The last lane, with no path back into the loop: reaching it means Task_IgPublisher succeeded on Lane_Qc's clean verdict. It does not itself decide whether the release is authorised: that call is draft-to-publication.bpmn's, and Task_PublishIg only executes what that separate process has already cleared."
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/processes/content/l3-fhir-pipeline.bpmn:99
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The QC reviewer rules on the aggregate QA against the publication gates. Emitting the QA report is mechanical; ruling on it is the reviewer's decision."
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/processes/content/l3-fhir-pipeline.bpmn:50
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The single gate between valid FHIR JSON and the full IG Publisher build: Task_IgPublisher runs only once this lane says clean, so a compiling-but-wrong profile never reaches a publishable IG."
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/processes/content/l3-fhir-pipeline.bpmn:42
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Two jobs share this lane. Task_Sushi and Task_Validate turn FSH into validated FHIR JSON and loop back to the modeller lane on failure with no bean filed: re-running compile-and-validate is cheap. Task_IgPublisher runs only once Lane_Qc has passed, and its output is what Lane_PubMgr publishes."
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/processes/content/l3-fhir-pipeline.bpmn:84
#. Diagram label
msgid "Validate against profiles"
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/processes/content/l3-fhir-pipeline.bpmn:85
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Validate the compiled resources against their profiles and the packages they constrain. A validator that could not start is could-not-determine, never a pass with an empty findings list. Failures return to authoring."
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/processes/content/l3-fhir-pipeline.bpmn:22
#. Diagram label
msgid "Work plan (beans)"
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/processes/content/l3-fhir-pipeline.bpmn:67
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Write the FSH profiles, value sets and definitions the source model calls for. This is the stage where profiles, slicing and invariants belong — a decision that can only be expressed in FHIR comes here, not back into the source model."
msgstr ""

